      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T09:46:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @jk@ozlabs.org.\nHow is an SOC with two USB host controllers handled? \nThe AST2600 has ehci0 at 1e6a1000 and ehci1 at 1e6a3000, so a device can sit at port chain 1.2.1 on each. Reading get_usb_specifier(), the bus number ahead of the \u0027-\u0027 is not part of the specifier, so I would expect both to want mcu1u2u1 - am I misreading it? udev\u0027s own ID_PATH for the same device does keep the host: platform-1e6a3000.usb-usb-0:1.2.1:1.0.",
      "parentUuid": "0ea7940e_6617ea47",
      "revId": "08c12c4a29a60212ea5686b05a9e2cc3b137ad36",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
